    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0694" n="582" xml:id="pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50A/127: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-15T12:00:00+08:00">May 15, 1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        May 15—4:52 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. Reliably reported that Haas<anchor n="93" xml:id="d556-f1"/> of League staff
                    here is planning, as maneuver against possible replacement of League experts by
                    Japanese advisers, the reorganization of League technical activities in China
                    including the assignment of more competent League personnel here to be under the
                    direction of a chief expert. It is stated that Chiang Kai-shek has not so far
                    been persuaded to more than a lukewarm attitude but Soong and Kung are said to
                    have agreed to the scheme.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d556-f1" n="93" xml:id="d556-f1-content">
                <p>Robert Haas, director of the Communications and Transit Section of the League of
                    Nations Secretariat.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
